      "extract": "[]{#intro label=\"intro\"} The merger of two white dwarfs has received considerable interest during the last years because it is thought to be at the origin of several interesting astrophysical phenomena. In particular, the coalescence of two white dwarfs is one of the possible scenarios --- the so-called double-degenerate scenario --- to account for Type Ia supernova outbursts (Webbink 1984; Iben & Tutukov 1984).",
