      "extract": "We have shown that the hot, convective, diﬀerentially rotating corona predicted by detailed three-dimensional simulations of the merger of two degenerate stellar cores is able to produce very high magnetic ﬁelds. We have also shown that these magnetic ﬁelds are conﬁned to the outer layers of the remnant of the coalescence, and do not propagate neither to the interior of the white dwarf or to the debris region. Our",
